  "worked_solution": "To find the complex conjugate of a vector, we take the complex conjugate of the entries of the vector. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{x} & =\\overset{\u2015}{[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1-10\\text{i} \\\\ -7-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{6} \\\\ \\overset{\u2015}{1-10\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{\u2015}{-7-3\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1+10\\text{i} \\\\ -7+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
